{
  "statement": "Ensuring ethical and compliance standards is crucial in a bookkeeping system to protect stakeholders and maintain trust. Requirement RES-01 guarantees adherence to financial regulations, while RES-02 ensures that only authorized personnel can modify transactions, promoting accountability. RES-03 provides a transparent audit trail for financial transactions, essential for integrity. RES-04 focuses on fraud detection, and RES-05 ensures compliance with accounting standards for fair reporting. RES-06 allows for confidential reporting of ethical concerns, while RES-07 assures fairness in multi-currency transactions. Without these, the system risks legal consequences and reputational damage.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-03"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "RES-03's requirement for a transparent audit trail may conflict with EFF-03's goal of minimizing memory usage by 30%, as extensive logging may require more resources."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["TRU-03"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "TRU-03's requirement for a minimum 5-year immutable audit trail conflicts with RES-01, which requires compliance with legal standards that may necessitate longer retention periods."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-04"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "The emphasis on thorough error handling in SAF-04 may conflict with RES-04's requirement to detect and alert users about discrepancies in a timely manner."
    }
  ],
